    "description": "Base coverage matrix mapping channels (rows) to event-type actions (columns) with the intended enforcement tier. This is the design-level intent at base-channel granularity. The deployed M/W/B policies in content/Policies/ collapse multiple actions per policy and decompose further by Authorized/Unauthorized — see docs/v0-policy-dataset-system/02-coverage-matrix.md for that view.",
    "tiers": {
      "M": "Monitor",
      "B": "Block"
    },
    "cell_encoding": {
      "M": "monitor tier intended",
      "B": "block tier intended",
      "none": "explicitly no coverage decided (CSV cell '-')",
      "null": "undefined / not specified (CSV cell empty)"
    },
    "global_column": "The 'Global' column is the channel-level umbrella tier — when set, it represents catch-all coverage for any action on that channel not otherwise specified."
